Insights (Business-Focused Risk Commentary)
A polished insights section for interviewers or reviewers.

## Insight 1 — Early arrears no longer signalling deterioration
DPD1 trended flat to slightly down across Apr–Jul, yet bad rate rose sharply in Jul–Aug.
This suggests:
ageing vintages flowing through, or
collections effectiveness issues

## Insight 2 — Credit tightening had a delayed stabilising effect
After Approval Rate dropped in Aug–Sep due to risk-based tightening, Bad Rate stabilised in Sep–Oct before improving in Nov.
This matches expected lag behaviour in lending portfolios.

## Insight 3 — Year-end uplift consistent with seasonal patterns
DPD1 and DPD30 increased in Dec due to:
higher utilisation
Xmas seasonal spend
higher missed-payments historically observed

No structural portfolio deterioration indicated.

## Insight 4 — Flow-through ratios signal benign risk environment
New30+ remained stable at 5–7% of early arrears.
This is consistent with:
adequate collections capacity
resilient economic backdrop
benign risk migration
